  "question": {
    "text": "The top of a water tank is open to air and its water level is maintained. It is giving out <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.74</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> water per minute through a circular opening of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math> radius in its wall. The depth of the centre of the opening from the level of water in the tank is close to:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2.9</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4.8</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6.0</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9.6</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0139_dcbb6d179ddf.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 133px;\" /></p><p>Volume of water flowing out<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>v</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is area of opening and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;is speed of water from the opening.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>Volume</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>v</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>74</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mi>min</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3.14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>H</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mi>min</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.74</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3.14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.8</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the height of water in the tank was&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;from the bottom of the tank.</p></blockquote>"
  }
